WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.840
SCP-682 Vs SCP-170. Can the&nbsp;
ultimate molecular superglue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.560
pin the Hard to Destroy Reptile down for good?

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.240
The SCP-170 glue was laced onto a series of metal&nbsp;
chains, with the hope of confining rather than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.200
executing the monster. The tissue sample was&nbsp;
promising, and things proceeded from there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.600
682 was sedated and wrapped with chains&nbsp;
which were then connected to the ground.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.880
Initially, when 682 woke up, it thrashed around&nbsp;
and tried to escape. However, its attempts were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.320
futile. But before the researchers could&nbsp;
start patting themselves on the back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.840
682 began to grow, until it reached such&nbsp;
a size that the chains simply popped off.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.840
The leading theory as to how this worked&nbsp;
was that it hadn’t technically grown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:48.640
but increased the distance between its particles,&nbsp;
shattering the molecular bond created by SCP-170.

